    "title": "Oldsmar man charged with lobster violations - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n9 hours ago\nLONG KEY — A 40-year-old Oldsmar man was arrested Saturday, Aug. 30, for multiple lobster violations, according to the Monroe County Sheriff's Office.\nMarine Deputy Willie Guerra was on patrol near the Channel Five Bridge at approximately 12:15 p.m. when he reported observing Alexander Alfonso Matos throw multiple lobster tails into the water.\nGuerra recovered multiple lobsters, two of which had puncture wounds consistent with being speared. A spear gun was also recovered from the water, reports say.\nAlfonso Matos was charged with possession of nine over-the-limit lobsters, possession of eight undersized lobsters, possession of two speared lobsters and possession of wrung tails in the water.\nHe was taken to jail.",
